-- A section GIVEN declares a name once for a whole section.
-- The taught spelling is on the line after the heading, indented past the §.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `applicable rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate that applies to this transaction
          surcharge IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2

@export Tax on an amount
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER @desc The amount being taxed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`tax on` amount MEANS
    amount TIMES `applicable rate` PLUS surcharge

-- Both rules below read `applicable rate` without re-declaring it.

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is above the threshold` MEANS
    `applicable rate` AT LEAST 0.2

-- A nested section may re-declare the name; that is a DIFFERENT name, and it
-- takes precedence only inside the child section.

§§ `Concessionary rates`
    GIVEN `applicable rate` IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`concessionary tax on` amount MEANS
    amount TIMES `applicable rate`

-- A column-1 GIVEN still lists the next declaration's own inputs.

§ `Ordinary signatures`

GIVEN quantity IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
doubled MEANS quantity TIMES 2
